.SH NAME
.PP
auto-nfs-client-setup - Configure host as an NFS client

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-nfs-client-setup sysctl|daemon domain
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
sysctl|daemon   Select a method to map usernames across client/server
domain          Domain for nfsuserd if using daemon for mapping
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-nfs-client-setup
command enables the necessary services (e.g. statd, lockd, nfsuserd)
for accessing remote NFS servers, and performs any other essential
configuration.

NFSv4 user mapping is enabled, to allow access to servers where
usernames match, but user IDs and group IDs may differ.  On FreeBSD,
this can be accomplished using sysctls without the need for daemons.
On other systems, the nfsuserd daemon must be running on server
and client.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-nfs-client-setup sysctl
auto-nfs-client-setup daemon our.domain
.ad
.fi

.SH FILES
.nf
.na

.ad
.fi

